---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import ReasoningEffortDemo from '../../components/ReasoningEffortDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Reasoning Effort" description="A pill slider for how hard a model thinks before it replies.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Reasoning Effort</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A pill-shaped slider that picks one of a few effort levels, such as Low, Medium, High, and Max. While you drag, a
    bubble grows out of the track and names the level.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <ReasoningEffortDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Reasoning Effort usage"
      code={`import { ReasoningEffort } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/reasoning-effort";

const levels = ["Quick", "Balanced", "Thorough", "Maximum"];
const [value, setValue] = useState(1);

<ReasoningEffort levels={levels} value={value} onValueChange={setValue} />`}
    />
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="In a model picker, with the model name in the bubble"
      code={`const effortLabel = { low: "Low", medium: "Medium", high: "High", max: "Max" };
const index = Math.max(0, model.efforts.indexOf(effort));

{model.efforts.length > 0 && (
  <ReasoningEffort
    label={model.label}
    levels={model.efforts.map((level) => effortLabel[level])}
    value={index}
    onValueChange={(next) => setEffort(model.efforts[next])}
  />
)}`}
    />
    <p>
      The slider is controlled: pass the chosen index as <code>value</code> and update it in <code>onValueChange</code>.
      It calls
      <code>onValueChange</code> as soon as a drag crosses into a new level, not only on release. Hide it when a model
      has no levels.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>levels</code>: level names from lowest to highest effort. Each one gets a tick, spaced evenly. Ticks grow
        taller toward higher effort.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>value</code>: the index of the chosen level.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>onValueChange</code>: called with the new index.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>label</code>: optional text before the level name in the bubble, such as the model name.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>aria-label</code> (default "Reasoning effort") or
        <code>aria-labelledby</code> names the slider.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>className</code>: added to the root.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The control is a fixed 256 × 52px: a 32px track with 20px above it for the bubble. It fits the 18rem picker
      popover with 16px from each outer edge: 15px of padding plus the popover's 1px border.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The track is one <code>role="slider"</code> tab stop. Its value is the index, and <code>aria-valuetext</code>{' '}
      reads the level name. Arrow keys move one level, and Home and End jump to the ends. Keyboard focus shows a 2px{' '}
      <code>--sprout-focus</code> outline.
    </p>
    <p>
      The bubble is hidden from screen readers because the value text already names the level. When reduced motion is
      requested, the thumb, bubble, and level change jump instead of tweening. In forced colors mode the track, fill,
      thumb, and ticks use system colors.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The fill uses <code>--sprout-primary</code>, so the opt-in TulipFarm theme tints it green. The pill and bubble
      shade from
      <code>--sprout-hover</code> to <code>--sprout-active</code> with a<code>--sprout-line</code> edge. The bubble's
      label uses
      <code>--sprout-text</code> and its level uses <code>--sprout-muted</code>. The thumb is white; override{' '}
      <code>--sprout-reasoning-effort-thumb</code>
      to change it.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
